since the massive hogwarts legacy  gameplay reveal at the sony state of  play back in march we've been frequently  treated to little updates along the way  like the asmr video technical  clarifications and even a sneak peek at  the character creator for the game but i  think a much bigger announcement is  coming soon like really soon avalanche  absolutely knocked it out of the park  with the gameplay revealed the little  social media updates have also been  fantastic but there's one major question  that keeps getting asked more and more  with every post they make and you all  already know the question when is the  release date i'll give you my prediction  and reasoning on when i think it will  hit but as for a release date  announcement i think it's coming very  soon maybe even before the end of this  month and here's why first we already  have confirmation that more new  information is coming before the end of  the summer back on may 19th hogwarts  legacy community manager chandler wood  tweeted can't believe it's already been  two months since the state of play i'm  really excited about what we're working  on right now we've got some pretty cool  stuff to show you later this summer  technically that could be as late as  mid-september for those of us in the  northern hemisphere and sure there's no  guarantee he was talking specifically  about a release date then again  september 1st is a pretty big day in the  harry potter series maybe we get a big  announcement then i could absolutely see  something then but there are some  additional factors that still make me  think a release announcement will happen  sooner than september 1st like god of  war ragnarok sony just revealed that god  of war will hit retail and digital  storefronts on november 9th 2022 but  wait what does god of war have to do  with hogwarts legacy well god of war  ragnarok is virtually guaranteed to be  one of the biggest games of the year and  is certain to be a huge seller its 2018  predecessor is the biggest selling ps4  title of all time with more than 20  million copies sold typically in the  video game industry publishers and  marketing teams try and avoid releasing  too close to other big blockbuster  titles if they can help it for some  games with radically different audiences  like say doom eternal and animal  crossing new horizons it's not as big of  a deal but for an action-adventure title  with rpg elements and iconic characters  there's going to be at least a decent  bit of audience overlap between hogwarts  legacy and god of war not to mention  that sony is heavily marketing hogwarts  legacy but with as much love as they're  showing it there's no doubt they're  gonna give god of war even more love so  it makes sense that wb would want to  give hogwarts legacy at least a little  bit of breathing room away from god of  war ragnarok is likely the big domino  that a number of publishers were waiting  to fall before they announced release  dates for their titles for spoken  despite being essentially finished very  quickly announced they're making a  strategic decision to push the game out  to january 24th 2023. starfield of  course has already been pushed out to  2023 and then we have a whole host of  other semi-big to big titles without  release dates like bayonetta 3 sonic  frontiers hogwarts legacy and plenty of  others the last official word we've  received is that hogwarts legacy is  slated for a holiday 2022 release which  typically means in either november or  december so quite frankly we're running  out of time if it's still on track for a  2022 release we're currently in early  july or roughly five months away from  december and you'd expect wb will win at  least a few months to build hype with a  more mainstream audience through tv  commercials web advertisements and  hopefully a collector's edition  announcement and of course important  pre-order details being communicated  ahead of time on any such edition we do  not want absolute pandemonium and mayhem  online like they had with ps5 pre-orders  so god of war announced an early  november release date in early july a  full four months ahead of release now  all games don't follow that same exact  rule but if wb and avalanche are looking  to release nsa in december i would think  they'll want to have the date confirmed  no later than early october but most  likely much sooner and even more so if  they're planning to release in november  speaking of the date itself though my  prediction remains tuesday december 6th  wb typically releases their games on  tuesdays and this would give hogwarts  legacy plenty of separation away from  wb's other big titles it also gives them  roughly a month separation from god of  war which being a first party title for  sony and featuring arguably its most  iconic character in kratos the game will  certainly receive a robust marketing  push from playstation and considering  that hogwarts legacy definitely appears  to have a marketing deal with  playstation i would expect they'll  encourage wb to give some space between  those two there and honestly wb would be  crazy to ignore such a request after all  playstation will be likely to be able to  devote even more resources to helping  promote hogwarts legacy the further out  they get from ragnarok's release date  just hopefully not too far out as in  like 2023 it certainly seems like  playstation is a big believer in  hogwarts legacy and plans to do whatever  they can to help push the title they  actually made a special trailer showing  off some of the unique features of the  duelson's controller for hogwarts legacy  i cover all those details in the video  here on the right side of your screen so  definitely check that one out next as  always thank you all so much for  watching and i'll talk to you again soon
 

